        "change": null,
        "said": "Issue #86 reports that the first factory read after a server start takes about 4.4 s. The reporter blames synchronous forge discovery or process spawning in changeMergeState (packages/adapters/src/forge-host.ts:194) for blocking the event loop, and proposes discovering forges once per process. I did not reproduce it. Reading the source, forgeHostDiscovery (lines 35-45) does an awaited config read, a path computation and sourceForgePlugins(), none of it visibly synchronous or heavy. The only Sync calls under packages/forge are in test fixtures. Discovery does run once per lookup, so up to 90 times for keys 1..90, and each lookup is followed by dispatchForge, which I did not read and which presumably spawns a plugin process. So a blocking spawn, or a burst of concurrent spawns, there or in the fan-out in packages/server/src/routes/api.factory.ts could be the real cause. Caching discovery is plausible but unproven. AGENTS.md requires reproducing a bug or establishing a concrete causal chain before editing. The pack's default triage policy defers to the project's own guidance and no project policy is named.",
